    ],
  },
        question: "The question this row carried: may the three production sites compare structurally, and where is that decided? While the wall stood the production fleet-converge entry (dag/gunbc/runner/runner_host_file_converge.dag) refused in RESOLVE at these sites (EqualityMemberUnjudgeable: CreateCause routed member inside a generic application at host_effect.dag, Measure sites at fleet_physical_inventory and compute_seat_ensure), so no fleet converge could run. The interim rewrites of #16045 (fleet) and #16099 (compute_seat_ensure, host_effect) closed that production refusal on main, and this row carried the record that they were interim and what their removal depended on. Each interim replaced a Measure comparison whose operands were same-unit by declaration (fleet: the declared sum and nominal_rackmount_units_declared were both RackUnit; rack: data rack_01_catalog_units IS navepoint_18u_open_frame_catalog.rack_units; seat: seat_fell_by declared before/after/granted all Kibibyte), which is why the measure_count cardinality comparison was faithful there -- measure_count names no units, so that faithfulness was a property of those declarations, not of the helper. The host_effect interim carried a drift risk the row recorded at the time: its hand-written match duplicated the constructor shape of data host_effect_converge_loop_evidence, so an edit to one spelling without the other would have classified the sentinel as OneShot instead of ConvergeLoop with no refusal. The named sentinel host_effect_apply_witness was not executable through the claim route at that pin (no import lines; resolve failed on the claim route; inventory in the retained 30-P-CAND.stderr), and it stayed unexecuted: the row claimed no executability either way. It remains rostered as an offline local recipe (WitnessExclusionRow in gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots, classification OfflineLocalRecipe), with no gate enrollment. The dependency this row named for removal was the root repair, which had itself been blocked by an E0369 synthesis regression in the emitted source_root_eval closure (v2-bootstrap 42414168425, E0369 Rc<DemandEngine<Rc<NativeDemandValue>>>, the occurrence-based pairing of #15992); that pairing was measured unsound and deleted, and the repair that landed judges each written type argument where the declaration's own parameter occurs. The three sites now read as plain structural '==' again and the interims are deleted: see the disposition and the closing sighting, which carry the executions.",
  sightings: FreeSemigroup {
    head: ConcernSighting {
      revision: "1bdf7152c79b56933e069a66db86293559b191b3",
      evidence: FreeSemigroup {
        head: CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.host.host_effect", decl_name: "host_effect_is_converge_loop_evidence") },
        tail: [],
      },
      account: "Observed subject: main at 1bdf7152c79b56933e069a66db86293559b191b3, clean local release build, binary sha256 acd2d80336c2ce7ac2ff23ec621d5c58a0a4027c47d0be793f2d727015359962 (receipt of quiet-raven-506 / fierce-gull-111): the production fleet-converge entry exits 1 at resolve refusing at fleet_physical_inventory Measure, host_effect CreateCause and compute_seat_ensure Measure. A second observation at 708057ca4b3a4eb046adab96e10586ccb6cb335c (sleek-wren-619, --dry-run resolve) refuses at the same three sites. The turn is between f6f57e7e16cc6b68b2d4e02e3de8adc7d2421996 (fleet run 42230507796 resolved the same entry) and these revisions; the identified trigger is withheld (source range vs build provenance open). The stopgap patch base 4aa7a03c48bb6a0819adfee2cca095fb6ddadea4 is the lineage base, NOT an observation subject. Stopgap prepared at the lane owner's request (keen-otter authorization via cool-badger routing).",
    },
    tail: [
      ConcernSighting {
        revision: "eeae4193aaf5a1d7054a80eb0100a850244378b0",
        evidence: FreeSemigroup {
          head: CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "equality_argument_by_target") },
          tail: [CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "is_unit_variant_phantom_argument") }],
        },
      account: "Closing read, measured at eeae4193aaf5 with a compiler built from that seed AND with the partition crates (src/v1/stage0_v1_infer, stage0_emit_core, stage0_std_surface) actually recompiled: the generated mirrors are pulled into those crates through #[path] includes outside their own src/, and a build that only rebuilds v1-compiler keeps the previously compiled rule -- that is how an earlier read on this branch reported these entries green while they still refused, and how a later read reported the shipped arms as failing specimens they in fact pass. Both of those reads are withdrawn. Measured with the crates recompiled, the two arms in the position they ship admit Holder<FooBarUnit> on a marker declared in the specimen module, Holder<RackUnitHeight>, Holder<Length>, Pair<Length, Nat> and the written Measure<Length, RackUnitHeight, Nat>, and the three entries that used to refuse each resolve with zero equality rows and zero resolve-failed headers; at 3d34fc61ca6e the same entries refused at host_effect_is_converge_loop_evidence, seat_fell_by and fleet_nominal_rackmount_arithmetic_holds. The only specimen refusals left are the alias-as-argument ones, recorded in their own row. The self-host instrument builds under rustc with zero E0369 where the previous head failed v2-bootstrap with E0369. The whole equality witness module runs 76 PASS and 4 FAIL, and those four fail identically under a compiler built from origin/main, so the repair admits the structural shapes without moving any refusal.",
      },
    ],
  },
  disposition: Integrated { evidence: IntegrationEvidence {
    integrated_at: "eeae4193aaf5a1d7054a80eb0100a850244378b0" as CommitSha,
    // The interim leaves this PR deletes, each cited at the revision that introduced it: #16099 rewrote the
    // host_effect CreateCause site and seat_fell_by, #16045 rewrote the fleet rackmount arithmetic. With the
